It is my first Saturday shift at the little café.
I have arrived early.
The sun is shining on the street in Copenhagen.
I am looking forward to it, but I am also a little nervous.
I have never worked in a café before.
I went into the back room to get ready.
On a table lay a new apron for me.
I put it on and tied it in the back.
It felt good to wear it.
Now I am ready to begin.
I have to learn to open the café correctly.
First, I unlocked the heavy front door.
Afterwards, I went out onto the pavement to get ready.
I carried four heavy iron chairs out.
I have placed them around a little table.
Now I just need the second chair for the next table.
In a little while, the other volunteers will arrive.
I am very excited about my first day.
